# Ocypus IOTA A62 CPU cooler - digital display
#
# The cooler's controller enumerates as USB 1a2c:434d "SEMICO USB Gaming
# Keyboard". Interface 0 is a (silent) boot keyboard; interface 1 carries the
# vendor-defined display report. Only the hidraw node of interface 1 is
# granted to the active seat user via the uaccess ACL, so a systemd user
# service can write to it. Nothing else changes; no 0666, no extra group.
#
# Must sort before 73-seat-late.rules (which applies the uaccess tag) and
# after 60-persistent-hidraw.rules (which sets ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM).
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a2c", ATTRS{idProduct}=="434d", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="01", TAG+="uaccess"
